{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to His heart.</b> At first He was grieved to His heart; now that He accepted the offerings, He said to His heart <b>I will not again</b>. According to the plain sense, one refers to the earth and the other refers to living creatures. And a proof for the matter: opposite it we find in the covenant of security: 'and all flesh shall not be cut off, and there shall never again be a flood to destroy.'" "<b>For the inclination of man's heart is evil from his youth.</b> On account of his youth and childhood he sins, and the inclination of his heart is evil, and I no longer have reason to punish him as I did."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:33.814107860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}